## API DEVELOPMENT RULES (CRITICAL)
- All APIs must live under `/app/api/v1/*`
- APIs must:
  - Validate authentication
  - Enforce `hospital_id` scoping
  - Enforce RBAC
- APIs must NOT:
  - Import UI components
  - Depend on browser APIs
  - Assume a web-only client

Example:
POST /api/v1/auth/super-admin/signup
POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email
GET /api/v1/branches

yaml
Copy code

---

## FRONTEND (SUPER ADMIN) RULES
- Frontend pages live under `(super-admin)`
- UI must consume backend APIs via HTTP
- Do NOT access database directly from pages
- Role-based UI rendering is REQUIRED
- Assume APIs may later move to a separate service

---

## MULTI-TENANCY RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- Every database query MUST include `hospital_id`
- Tenant context comes from authenticated token
- Super Admin:
  - Can see all branches
  - Does NOT see itself as a branch
- Branch Manager:
  - Can only see assigned branch
- SYSTEM_ADMIN:
  - Can see all hospitals (platform-level)

No cross-hospital data access is allowed.

---

## SUPER ADMIN CREATION FLOW (MANDATORY)
- Super Admin is created via API
- Email verification is REQUIRED before activation
- Flow:
  1. Signup → status = PENDING
  2. Email token sent
  3. Token verified
  4. Account activated

Required fields:
- hospital_name
- admin_name
- admin_email (global unique)
- password (hashed)
- hospital_type (single | multi)

---

## BRANCH RULES
- Every hospital MUST have at least one branch
- Single hospitals still create exactly one branch
- Branch fields:
  - branch_name
  - hospital_id
  - address
  - phone
  - email
  - is_head_branch

---

## AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY
- JWT access tokens (short-lived)
- Refresh tokens (secure storage)
- Web: HTTP-only cookies
- Mobile: Authorization header
- Password hashing: bcrypt
- Rate limit auth endpoints
- Enforce HTTPS assumptions

---

## DATABASE RULES
- PostgreSQL only
- UUID primary keys
- Indexed:
  - hospital_id
  - branch_id
- Soft deletes where applicable
- Audit fields:
  - created_at
  - updated_at
  - created_by

---

## ERROR HANDLING & LOGGING
- Centralized error handling
- No raw stack traces in production
- Structured logging with tenant context
- Clear API error responses

---

## WHAT CURSOR MUST NEVER DO
- Do NOT mix UI and business logic
- Do NOT bypass RBAC
- Do NOT create tenant-unscoped queries
- Do NOT assume single-hospital logic
- Do NOT expose PII in logs

---

## FUTURE-PROOFING
- Design for:
  - AI medical assistants
  - Insurance integrations
  - Pharmacy & lab modules
  - Multi-language support
- APIs must remain stable and versioned

---

## EXPECTED OUTPUT
- Enterprise-grade SaaS code
- Secure, scalable, multi-tenant
- Mobile-ready backend
- Clean separation of concerns